From 1d778699e4ccca6faafed98f375c836159862253 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FerrionOS <noreply@ferrionos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:45:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] layout: Tile the windows of a free workspace (F7)

A floating window of a free workspace can be tiled, as on the Mac: to
a half, a quarter, the whole working area (Fill, which leaves the bar
and the dock) or its middle, with the new `tile-floating-window`
action. It remembers the place and size it had before the first
tiling, which `untile-floating-window` returns it to.

The keys that move a window keep their verb on a free workspace, as
the design's shortcut table asks: move-column-left and -right tile to
that half, move-window-up fills, move-window-down returns, and
maximize-column fills or returns. On a columns workspace they are
niri's.

Dragging a floating window of a free workspace so that the pointer is
within 16 pixels of a side edge draws niri's insert hint as the outline
of that half, and dropping it there tiles it.


Agent-written tests and their test-only helpers were removed under ADR 0025.
The source commit in the header records the original patch provenance;
this patch is regenerated against the preceding test-free stage. Upstream
tests remain, with the config snapshots adapted to the production fields.
